  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "kjzqfpy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "MOTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Motion is defined as a change in position relative to time and a reference point.",
        "Distance measures total path covered (scalar), whereas displacement measures the shortest path between initial and final points (vector).",
        "Acceleration is the rate of change of velocity; negative acceleration is termed retardation.",
        "The three core equations of motion are v = u + at, s = ut + ½at², and v² = u² + 2as.",
        "On a Velocity-Time graph, the slope indicates acceleration and the area under the curve indicates distance."
      ],
      "id": "6km5ok4"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Equations of Motion",
          "value": "3",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "SI Unit of Acceleration",
          "value": "m/s²",
          "icon": "info"
        },
        {
          "label": "km/h to m/s Factor",
          "value": "5/18",
          "icon": "clock"
        },
        {
          "label": "Minimum Displacement",
          "value": "0",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "lwxsamy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Motion is said to occur when an object changes its position with respect to time and a reference point.If an object does not change its position with time, it is said to be at rest.",
      "id": "rd91nqf"
    },
    {
      "id": "x532po3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "REST AND MOTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "3v8g5v5",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Rest: When an object does not change its position with time.</li><li>Motion: When an object changes its position with time.</li></ul>",
        "Rest: When an object does not change its position with time.",
        "Motion: When an object changes its position with time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example:",
      "id": "37nbmjj"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A person sitting in a bus is at rest with respect to the bus but in motion with respect to the road.",
      "id": "gm8yknp"
    },
    {
      "id": "svqdxxw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF MOTION"
    },
    {
      "id": "k1qj0wx",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Rectilinear Motion – Motion in a straight line",
        "Circular Motion – Motion in a circular path",
        "Rotational Motion – Motion about an axis",
        "Oscillatory Motion – To and fro motion"
      ]
    },
