      "content": "UNITS AND CONVERSIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "SI Units Frequently Tested: Acceleration is m/s², while Speed and Velocity are m/s.",
        "Graph Interpretation: In Velocity-Time graphs, Slope = Acceleration and Area = Distance.",
        "Speed Conversion: To convert km/h to m/s, multiply by 5/18; to convert m/s to km/h, multiply by 18/5.",
        "Vector vs Scalar Property: Displacement can be zero, whereas Distance is always positive."
      ],
      "id": "1rstiow"
    },
